      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T23:48:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the the contact group name and protocol relates bus segments over a connector. For any two boards that connect via a given port it\u0027s required that the set of contact groups from each board\u0027s port definition are equivalent with respect to each element\u0027s `Name` and `Protocol` properties.\n\n\nThe contact group coupling is what prevents considering a relationship between bus segments I2C12 and USB1 for instance (the \"USB Port B\" segment on \"BMC Board\" relates to the \"USB1\" segment on \"Peripheral Board\" because the \"Segment\" property of the \"USB1\" contact group on \"BMC Port\" of each board relates to each segment respectively).\n\nDo you feel I need to integrate this explanation into the text somewhere? If so, where do you think is best?",
      "parentUuid": "20993845_117595b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 443,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 445,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "6f2056d979eaecacc535cdf0b7214fa9847cd32f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
